  "title": "Song of Solomon 1",
  "display_title": "Song of Solomon 1",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "song-of-solomon",
  "book": "Song of Solomon",
  "bookName": "Song of Solomon",
  "bookOrder": 22,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 22001,
  "verseCount": 17,
  "aliases": [
    "Song",
    "Song of Songs",
    "SOS",
    "Canticles"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The song of songs, which is Solomon’s.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth: for thy love is better than wine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Because of the savour of thy good ointments thy name is as ointment poured forth, therefore do the virgins love thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Draw me, we will run after thee: the king hath brought me into his chambers: we will be glad and rejoice in thee, we will remember thy love more than wine: the upright love thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "I am black, but comely, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Look not upon me, because I am black, because the sun hath looked upon me: my mother’s children were angry with me; they made me the keeper of the vineyards; but mine own vineyard have I not kept.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth, where thou feedest, where thou makest thy flock to rest at noon: for why should I be as one that turneth aside by the flocks of thy companions?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "If thou know not, O thou fairest among women, go thy way forth by the footsteps of the flock, and feed thy kids beside the shepherds’ tents.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "I have compared thee, O my love, to a company of horses in Pharaoh’s chariots.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Thy cheeks are comely with rows of jewels, thy neck with chains of gold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "We will make thee borders of gold with studs of silver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "While the king sitteth at his table, my spikenard sendeth forth the smell thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "A bundle of myrrh is my well-beloved unto me; he shall lie all night betwixt my breasts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "My beloved is unto me as a cluster of camphire in the vineyards of Engedi.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair; thou hast doves’ eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Behold, thou art fair, my beloved, yea, pleasant: also our bed is green.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The beams of our house are cedar, and our rafters of fir.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:1:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
